    with_total(items, target, i + 1, path, total, results)

results = []
with_total([1, 2, 3, 4], 5, 0, [], 0, results)
print(results)
```
wrong[[[2, 3], [1, 4]]]: Subsets with 1 in are explored first, so [1, 4] is found before [2, 3].
